    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: cayley-hamilton-oq-02-oq-01\n\nInsights accumulated during research on this problem.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n[Initial observations about the problem will be recorded here]\n\n---\n\n## Insights\n\n[Insights from research attempts will be accumulated here]\n\n---\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n[Approaches known not to work will be documented here]\n\n---\n\n## Session 2026-07-02 (Session 1, researcher-15) — Algebraic core VERIFIED\n\n**Mode**: FRESH | **Outcome**: progress (verified partial result shipped)\n\n### What I Did\n- Chose Approach A (ODE-uniqueness) from problem.md and isolated its purely-algebraic\n  prerequisites, which need no analysis and can be shipped now.\n- Wrote `proofs/Proofs/CayleyHamiltonOQ02OQ01.lean` (namespace `PutzerMatrixExp`),\n  built GREEN via docker (Proofs.CayleyHamiltonOQ02OQ01), 0 sorries, 0 axioms.\n- Created gallery entry `src/data/proofs/cayley-hamilton-oq-02-oq-01/` (meta + annotations).\n- PR #33617 (branch research/cayley-hamilton-oq0201-putzer-core, label `research`).\n\n### Key Findings / Insights\n- **CommMonoid obstruction**: ρ_k = ∏_{i<k}(A-λ_i•1) CANNOT be a `Finset.prod` — matrix\n  multiplication is noncommutative so Matrix n n R is not a CommMonoid. Must define ρ by\n  ordered recursion ρ_0=1, ρ_{k+1}=ρ_k·(A-λ_k•1). This was the first (failed) build's error.\n- **Bridge trick**: prove ρ_k = aeval A (∏_{i<k}(X - C λ_i)) by induction; the product now\n  lives in R[X] (COMMUTATIVE), so Finset.prod_range_succ + map_mul apply and matrix\n  noncommutativity is confined to one map_mul per step. Then ρ_n = aeval A χ_A = 0.\n- Telescoping identity A·ρ_k = ρ_{k+1} + λ_k•ρ_k proved via commute_A_rho (induction, using\n  Commute.mul_right) + mul_sub/mul_smul_comm + abel.\n- Everything holds over an arbitrary CommRing R; only the deferred analytic layer needs ℝ/ℂ.\n\n### Built Items (all in Proofs/CayleyHamiltonOQ02OQ01.lean)\n- `rho` (def), `rho_zero`, `rho_succ`, `commute_A_factor`, `commute_A_rho`, `A_comm_rho`,\n  `A_mul_rho` (telescoping), `aeval_X_sub_C`, `rho_eq_aeval_prod`, `rho_card` (ρ_n = 0).\n\n### Next Steps (analytic layer — the remaining open part)\n1. Construct P_k : ℝ → ℂ with the triangular ODE derivative relations (iterated exponential\n   convolutions), prove HasDerivAt for each.\n2. Prove HasDerivAt (fun t => Σ_k P_k t • ρ_{k-1}) (A · M t) t via HasDerivAt.sum/.smul +\n   A_mul_rho + rho_card (boundary term vanishes).\n3. Package Mathlib ODE_solution_unique for matrix-valued ℝ → M_n(ℂ): vector field M ↦ A·M\n   is Lipschitz (‖A‖_op); conclude M(t) = NormedSpace.exp ℝ (t•A).\n   Good Aristotle candidate once P_k infra exists (KNOWN result).\n"
  },
